{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id341357605"}, "name":{"label":"Jhayesco"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-09-03T05:57:46-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"6.8.0"}, "id":{"label":"14505581502"}, "title":{"label":"Better than most but needs work"}, "content":{"label":"I purchased the paid version of this app after my Apple weather app failed to alert me to several serious weather events. The alerts on Carrot generally work well, and the precision is fairly good (overestimates rainfall from what I can see). But my main complaint is a glitch that could lead to significant safety issues. Half the time, when I click on the alerts, even though I know there are more than one, only one shows up. The app keeps the others hidden behind the first one, which means I might never see that there’s a severe thunderstorm warning for my area, for example. I have to navigate to a second weather app (weather channel) to be sure I’m seeing all the alerts. I find this unacceptable for a paid app. I don’t think I’ll be renewing my subscription after it ends for this reason, unless the glitch is fixed. But the sad truth is there are no truly great weather apps out there. This one spends lots of time on the weird “funny” stuff but can’t get the weather alerts right enough to be worth it. Still better than most. Dark Sky was the best and Apple killed it for no good reason, only to replace it with junk.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=961390574&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
